From 3d63382929f6a0a3b691f59dc6ceb70c65eb240d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 17:09:15 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] car-audio: bridge the HFP far-end voice onto the call bus

When the head unit is the hands-free (HFP client) side of a call, the far-end
voice arrives as an AUDIO_DEVICE_IN_BLUETOOTH_SCO_HEADSET input, and nothing
in the platform routes an input to a speaker. CarAudioService now creates an
audio patch from that input to the call bus -- USAGE_VOICE_COMMUNICATION,
resolved through the car zone configuration -- when the device appears,
releases it when the device goes away, and lets go of it when the service
tears its callbacks down.

The SCO input's runtime port carries no gain controller, so
AudioManagerHelper.createAudioPatch() accepts a source without one when the
requested gain is 0 and patches it at unity; a non-zero gain on such a source
stays an error. releaseAudioPatch() also returns after a successful release
instead of falling through to its "found no match" error.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 .../car/builtin/media/AudioManagerHelper.java |  43 ++++--
 .../android/car/audio/CarAudioService.java    | 128 ++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 163 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/car-builtin-lib/src/android/car/builtin/media/AudioManagerHelper.java b/car-builtin-lib/src/android/car/builtin/media/AudioManagerHelper.java
index aa4bc2671b..9c2e3323f1 100644
--- a/car-builtin-lib/src/android/car/builtin/media/AudioManagerHelper.java
+++ b/car-builtin-lib/src/android/car/builtin/media/AudioManagerHelper.java
@@ -185,17 +185,44 @@ public final class AudioManagerHelper {
                 AudioFormat.CHANNEL_OUT_DEFAULT, AudioFormat.ENCODING_DEFAULT, null);
         Slogf.d(TAG, "createAudioPatch sinkConfig: " + sinkConfig);
 
-        // Configure the source port to match the output port except for a gain adjustment
-        AudioGain audioGain = Objects.requireNonNull(getAudioGain(sourceDevice.getPort()),
-                "Gain controller not available for source port");
-
-        // size of gain values is 1 in MODE_JOINT
-        AudioGainConfig audioGainConfig = audioGain.buildConfig(AudioGain.MODE_JOINT,
-                audioGain.channelMask(), new int[] { gainInMillibels }, 0);
+        // Configure the source port to match the output port except for a gain adjustment.
+        //
+        // A SOURCE WITHOUT A GAIN CONTROLLER IS ALLOWED. The HFP far-end voice reaches the
+        // call bus through exactly such a patch on this board. The SCO input port is created
+        // dynamically when the phone connects, and that runtime instance carries no gains even
+        // when the declared port has one (2026-09-19, dumpsys media.audio_policy: a JOINT gain
+        // declared on "BT SCO Headset Mic" was listed on the declared port, not on the attached
+        // instance), so this board's policy declares none. getAudioGain() therefore threw
+        // "Audio device must have gains defined", CarAudioService caught it and logged
+        // "Could not bridge HFP SCO input <mac> onto the call bus", and the call carried on
+        // with no audio route -- a permanent silent no-op. Measured 2026-09-19: the controller
+        // delivered 13030 SCO packets, 90.6% of the payload non-zero, while the HDMI stream
+        // carried real-time digital silence for the whole call.
+        //
+        // The native layer imposes no such requirement: AudioPolicyManager::createAudioPatch
+        // builds the software bridge whether or not the source has a gain controller
+        // (frameworks/av/services/audiopolicy/managerdefault/AudioPolicyManager.cpp:6058-6068).
+        // A non-zero gain still needs a controller, so that case stays an error rather than
+        // being silently ignored; CarAudioService passes 0 for the HFP bridge.
+        AudioDevicePort sourcePort = Preconditions.checkNotNull(sourceDevice.getPort(),
+                "Source device [%s] does not contain an audio port", sourceDevice);
+        AudioGainConfig audioGainConfig = null;
+        if (sourcePort.gains().length > 0) {
+            AudioGain audioGain = Objects.requireNonNull(getAudioGain(sourcePort),
+                    "Gain controller not available for source port");
+            // size of gain values is 1 in MODE_JOINT
+            audioGainConfig = audioGain.buildConfig(AudioGain.MODE_JOINT,
+                    audioGain.channelMask(), new int[] { gainInMillibels }, 0);
+        } else if (gainInMillibels != 0) {
+            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Source port has no gain controller, cannot"
+                    + " apply " + gainInMillibels + " mB: " + sourceDevice);
+        } else {
+            Slogf.d(TAG, "createAudioPatch: source has no gain controller, patching at unity");
+        }
         // Construct an empty / default configuration excepts gain config here and it's up to the
         // audio HAL how to interpret this configuration, which the audio HAL
         // implementation should ignore.
-        AudioPortConfig sourceConfig = sourceDevice.getPort().buildConfig(0,
+        AudioPortConfig sourceConfig = sourcePort.buildConfig(0,
                 AudioFormat.CHANNEL_IN_DEFAULT, AudioFormat.ENCODING_DEFAULT, audioGainConfig);
 
         // Create an audioPatch to connect the two ports
